@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `law08-vintage`
IMPORT `law08-nouns`
IMPORT `law08-ch3-scope`

-- Chuong II, Muc 1 (Dieu 15-32): general provisions on the contract of insurance.
-- Law 139/2025/QH15 does not touch these articles: each rule has one arm. Where an article
-- refers to Dieu 63(3), which Law 139/2025/QH15 does change, the reference resolves in all
-- vintages and the called rule has its own arms (law08-ch3-scope.l4).
-- Periods counted in days are calendar days and a year is a calendar year: the Law does not say
-- (NOTES.md, fork F1). A contract term fixed by agreement is an input.

§ `Chuong II: Hop dong bao hiem`

§§ `Dieu 15: the contract of insurance`

@@q 370 377
@ref Dieu 15 (src:370-377)
GIVEN c IS A `A class of insurance contract`
GIVETH A `A type of insurance`
`Dieu 15(1): the type of insurance the class of contract belongs to` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `a life insurance contract`       THEN `life insurance`
    WHEN `a health insurance contract`     THEN `health insurance`
    WHEN `a property insurance contract`   THEN `non-life insurance`
    WHEN `a damage insurance contract`     THEN `non-life insurance`
    WHEN `a liability insurance contract`  THEN `non-life insurance`

-- Dieu 15(2). The parties may make one class or combine several, so long as the combination is
-- consistent with Dieu 63(3) (the insurer's one-type rule, with its exceptions).
@@q 378 381
@ref Dieu 15 (src:378-381)
GIVEN k IS A `A combination of classes`
      b IS A `The business of an insurer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 15(2): the classes combined are consistent with Dieu 63(3)` k b MEANS
    (NOT null (k's `classes combined`)) AND `Dieu 63(3): the business combines only the types of insurance the Law permits` b

-- Dieu 15(3)-(4). A marine insurance contract follows the Maritime Code, and this Law for what
-- the Code does not provide; any other matter this Law does not provide goes to the Civil Code.
-- The two inputs say whether the instrument "provides" for the matter: a question of the
-- instrument, not of the facts.
@@q 382 386
@ref Dieu 15 (src:382-386)
GIVEN c IS A `A contract of insurance`
      `the Maritime Code provides for the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this Law provides for the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A governing instrument`
`Dieu 15(3)-(4): the instrument that governs the matter` c `the Maritime Code provides for the matter` `this Law provides for the matter` MEANS
    BRANCH IF c's `is a maritime insurance contract` AND `the Maritime Code provides for the matter` THEN `the Maritime Code`
           IF `this Law provides for the matter` THEN `this Law`
           OTHERWISE `the Civil Code`

§§ `Dieu 16: principles`

@@q 388 408
@ref Dieu 16 (src:388-408)
`Dieu 16 — principles of making and performing the contract: utmost good faith (1), insurable interest (2), indemnity (3), subrogation (4), fortuity (5); (2) is applied by Dieu 34 and 44, (3) and (4) by the rules below (statement; no further rule evaluated)` MEANS
    "The principles of utmost good faith, insurable interest, indemnity, subrogation and fortuity."

@@q 399 401
@ref Dieu 16 (src:399-401)
GIVEN k IS A `A compensation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 16(3): the compensation respects the indemnity principle` k MEANS
    k's `compensation` AT MOST k's `actual loss in the insured event` OR k's `the contract agrees otherwise`

@@q 402 406
@ref Dieu 16 (src:402-406)
GIVEN c IS A `A class of insurance contract`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 16(4): the subrogation principle applies to the class` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `a life insurance contract`       THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a health insurance contract`     THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `Dieu 17: contents of the contract`

@@q 410 422
@ref Dieu 17 (src:410-422)
GIVEN k IS A `The contents of a contract`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 17(1): the contract states the essential contents` k MEANS
        k's `states the policyholder, the insured person, the beneficiary if any and the insurer`
    AND k's `states the object of insurance`
    AND k's `states the sum insured or the value of insured property or the limit of liability`
    AND k's `states the scope or benefits of insurance and the rules, conditions and terms`
    AND k's `states the rights and obligations of the insurer and the policyholder`
    AND k's `states the insurance term and when the contract takes effect`
    AND k's `states the premium and the method of paying it`
    AND k's `states the method of paying compensation or the insurance money`
    AND k's `states the method of resolving disputes`

@@q 425 426
@ref Dieu 17 (src:425-426)
GIVEN c IS A `A class of insurance contract`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 17(2): the Minister of Finance's detailed rules on contents for the class` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `a life insurance contract`       THEN REFUSE "Dieu 17(2) delegates the detail of the contents of life and health contracts to the Minister of Finance; the Minister's circular is not among the sources"
    WHEN `a health insurance contract`     THEN REFUSE "Dieu 17(2) delegates the detail of the contents of life and health contracts to the Minister of Finance; the Minister's circular is not among the sources"
    OTHERWISE REFUSE "Dieu 17(2) delegates only life and health contracts; for the other classes the Law has no detailed rule to refer to"

§§ `Dieu 18: form and evidence`

@@q 428 430
@ref Dieu 18 (src:428-430)
GIVEN f IS A `The form of a contract`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 18: the contract is in the form the Law requires` f MEANS
    f's `is made in writing`

@@q 428 430
@ref Dieu 18 (src:428-430)
GIVEN f IS A `The form of a contract`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 18: the making of the contract is evidenced` f MEANS
        f's `evidenced by the contract itself`
    OR  f's `evidenced by a certificate of insurance`
    OR  f's `evidenced by an insurance application or policy`
    OR  f's `evidenced by another form the law provides`

§§ `Dieu 19: exclusion clauses`

-- Dieu 19(1) defines the clause; Dieu 19(2) is what the insurer must do when the contract has one.
@@q 432 440
@ref Dieu 19 (src:432-440)
GIVEN e IS AN `An exclusion clause`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 19(2): the insurer has done what it must about the exclusion clause` e MEANS
    NOT e's `the contract has an exclusion clause`
    OR (    e's `the contract states the exclusion clearly`
        AND e's `the insurer explained the exclusion clearly and fully`
        AND e's `there is evidence the policyholder was given the explanation and understood it`)

-- Dieu 19(3). The insurer may not apply an exclusion for late notice when force majeure or an
-- objective obstacle caused the policyholder's delay.
@@q 441 444
@ref Dieu 19 (src:441-444)
GIVEN e IS AN `An exclusion clause`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 19(3): the late-notice exclusion may not be applied` e MEANS
    e's `the exclusion is for late notice` AND e's `force majeure or an objective obstacle caused the policyholder to notify the insured event late`

§§ `Dieu 20: rights and duties of the insurer`

@@q 447 465
@ref Dieu 20 (src:447-465)
GIVETH A LIST OF `A right of the insurer`
`Dieu 20(1): the rights of the insurer` MEANS
    LIST `to collect premium as the contract agrees`
       , `to require the policyholder to give full and truthful information`
       , `to rescind under Dieu 22(2) or terminate unilaterally under Dieu 26`
       , `to refuse to pay when outside the insurance liability or excluded`
       , `to require loss prevention and limitation measures`
       , `to require a third person to reimburse what it paid`
       , `another right the law gives`

@@q 466 489
@ref Dieu 20 (src:466-489)
GIVETH A LIST OF `A duty of the insurer`
`Dieu 20(2): the duties of the insurer` MEANS
    LIST `to give the policyholder the application, questionnaire, object details and rules, conditions and terms`
       , `to explain benefits, exclusions and the policyholder's rights and duties clearly and fully`
       , `to give the policyholder the evidence of the contract`
       , `to issue a receipt for premium`
       , `to compensate or pay when the insured event occurs`
       , `to explain a refusal to pay in writing`
       , `to cooperate with the policyholder on a third person's claim`
       , `to keep the contract records as the law provides`
       , `to keep the policyholder's and insured person's information confidential`
       , `another duty the law gives`

-- Dieu 20(1)(d): the insurer may refuse to pay when the event is outside its liability or excluded.
@@q 456 458
@ref Dieu 20 (src:456-458)
GIVEN h IS AN `An insurer's handling of a claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 20(1)(d): the insurer may refuse to pay` h MEANS
    (NOT h's `the event is within the insurer's liability under the contract`) OR h's `an exclusion of liability in the contract applies`

-- Dieu 20(2)(dd): the insurer must pay when the insured event occurs (not where it may refuse).
@@q 478 478
@ref Dieu 20 (src:478)
GIVEN h IS AN `An insurer's handling of a claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 20(2)(dd): the insurer is bound to pay` h MEANS
    h's `the event is within the insurer's liability under the contract` AND NOT h's `an exclusion of liability in the contract applies`

GIVEN h IS AN `An insurer's handling of a claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 20(2)(dd): the insurer's refusal is a breach` h MEANS
    h's `the insurer refused to pay` AND `Dieu 20(2)(dd): the insurer is bound to pay` h

-- Dieu 20(2)(e): a refusal must be explained in writing.
@@q 479 479
@ref Dieu 20 (src:479)
GIVEN h IS AN `An insurer's handling of a claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 20(2)(e): the refusal was not explained in writing` h MEANS
    h's `the insurer refused to pay` AND NOT h's `the insurer explained the refusal in writing`

-- Dieu 20(2)(g): cooperate on a third person's claim for a loss within the insurance liability.
@@q 480 482
@ref Dieu 20 (src:480-482)
GIVEN h IS AN `An insurer's handling of a claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 20(2)(g): the insurer failed to cooperate on the third person's claim` h MEANS
    h's `a third person claimed compensation from the policyholder for a loss within the insurance liability` AND NOT h's `the insurer cooperated with the policyholder in settling the third person's claim`

-- Dieu 20(2)(i): confidentiality, except at a competent State body's request or with agreement.
@@q 486 488
@ref Dieu 20 (src:486-488)
GIVEN h IS AN `An insurer's handling of a claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 20(2)(i): the insurer disclosed information in breach of confidentiality` h MEANS
    h's `the insurer disclosed the policyholder's or insured person's information` AND (NOT h's `a competent State body required the disclosure`) AND (NOT h's `the policyholder or insured person agreed to the disclosure`)

§§ `Dieu 21: rights and duties of the policyholder`

@@q 491 511
@ref Dieu 21 (src:491-511)
GIVETH A LIST OF `A right of the policyholder`
`Dieu 21(1): the rights of the policyholder` MEANS
    LIST `to choose the insurer`
       , `to ask for the application, questionnaire, object details and terms and for their explanation`
       , `to ask for the evidence of the contract`
       , `to ask for a receipt for premium`
       , `to rescind under Dieu 22(3) and Dieu 35 or terminate unilaterally under Dieu 26`
       , `to ask the insurer to compensate or pay when the insured event occurs`
       , `to transfer the contract`
       , `another right the law gives`

@@q 512 534
@ref Dieu 21 (src:512-534)
GIVETH A LIST OF `A duty of the policyholder`
`Dieu 21(2): the duties of the policyholder` MEANS
    LIST `to declare fully and truthfully what the insurer asks`
       , `to read and understand the terms`
       , `to pay premium in full and on time`
       , `to notify circumstances that increase or reduce the risk`
       , `to notify the insured event and cooperate in the loss adjustment`
       , `to take loss prevention and limitation measures`
       , `another duty the law gives`

@@q 521 522
@ref Dieu 21 (src:521-522)
GIVEN p IS A `The policyholder's conduct`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 21(2)(c): the policyholder failed to pay premium in full and on time` p MEANS
    p's `premium was due` AND NOT p's `premium was paid in full by the agreed time`

@@q 523 527
@ref Dieu 21 (src:523-527)
GIVEN p IS A `The policyholder's conduct`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 21(2)(d): the policyholder failed to notify a change of risk` p MEANS
    p's `a circumstance increasing or reducing the risk arose` AND p's `the contract agrees the policyholder is to notify such a circumstance` AND NOT p's `the policyholder notified the circumstance`

@@q 528 531
@ref Dieu 21 (src:528-531)
GIVEN p IS A `The policyholder's conduct`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 21(2)(dd): the policyholder failed to notify the insured event or cooperate` p MEANS
    p's `an insured event occurred` AND ((NOT p's `the policyholder notified the insured event as the contract agrees`) OR (NOT p's `the policyholder cooperated in the loss adjustment`))

§§ `Dieu 22: duty to give information, and the consequences of breaching it`

-- Dieu 22(1) is the mutual duty; (2) and (3) the consequence of a deliberate breach by each side.
@@q 537 542
@ref Dieu 22 (src:537-542)
`Dieu 22(1) — duty of each side to give information at the making of the contract (statement; applied by Dieu 22(2), 22(3) and 14(2)(d))` MEANS
    "The insurer gives full and accurate information and explains the terms; the policyholder gives full and truthful information about the object of insurance."

@@q 543 553
@ref Dieu 22 (src:543-553)
GIVEN d IS A `The disclosure at formation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 22(2): the insurer may rescind the contract` d MEANS
    d's `policyholder deliberately gave incomplete or false information to make the contract in order to be paid`

-- The insurer need not pay and must refund the premium less the reasonable costs the contract
-- allows; the policyholder must make good the insurer's damage. A refund cannot be negative (F7).
@@q 546 553
@ref Dieu 22 (src:546-553)
GIVEN d IS A `The disclosure at formation`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Dieu 22(2): the premium the insurer must refund` d MEANS
    IF NOT d's `policyholder deliberately gave incomplete or false information to make the contract in order to be paid`
    THEN REFUSE "Dieu 22(2) applies only where the policyholder deliberately gave incomplete or false information to be paid"
    ELSE IF d's `reasonable costs the contract allows to be deducted` AT MOST d's `premium paid`
         THEN d's `premium paid` MINUS d's `reasonable costs the contract allows to be deducted`
         ELSE REFUSE "Dieu 22(2) says nothing on reasonable costs above the premium paid"

@@q 554 559
@ref Dieu 22 (src:554-559)
GIVEN d IS A `The disclosure at formation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 22(3): the policyholder may rescind the contract` d MEANS
    d's `insurer deliberately failed to give, or gave false, information in order to make the contract`

GIVEN d IS A `The disclosure at formation`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Dieu 22(3): the premium the insurer must refund` d MEANS
    IF d's `insurer deliberately failed to give, or gave false, information in order to make the contract`
    THEN d's `premium paid`
    ELSE REFUSE "Dieu 22(3) applies only where the insurer deliberately failed to give information or gave false information"

§§ `Dieu 23: a change in the insured risk`

-- Dieu 23(1) and (3): what the policyholder may ask for if the risk fell, what the insurer may do
-- if it rose. Both depend on the contract providing for adjustment.
@@q 561 568
@@q 574 583
@ref Dieu 23 (src:561-568; src:574-583)
GIVEN c IS A `A change in the insured risk`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A request on a fall in the risk`
`Dieu 23(1): what the policyholder may ask for` c MEANS
    IF c's `the factors the premium is based on changed so that the insured risk fell` AND c's `the contract provides for adjustment on such a change`
    THEN LIST `reduce the premium for the remaining time`
            , `increase the sum insured for the remaining time`
            , `extend the insurance term`
            , `widen the scope of insurance for the remaining time`
    ELSE EMPTY

GIVEN c IS A `A change in the insured risk`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A measure on a rise in the risk`
`Dieu 23(3): what the insurer may do` c MEANS
    IF c's `the factors the premium is based on changed so that the insured risk rose` AND c's `the contract provides for adjustment on such a change`
    THEN LIST `recalculate the premium for the remaining time`
            , `reduce the sum insured for the remaining time`
            , `shorten the insurance term`
            , `narrow the scope of insurance for the remaining time`
    ELSE EMPTY

-- Dieu 23(2): if the insurer refuses the request, the policyholder may terminate, but must give
-- immediate written notice. Dieu 23(4): the insurer's right if the policyholder refuses.
@@q 569 573
@ref Dieu 23 (src:569-573)
GIVEN c IS A `A change in the insured risk`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 23(2): the policyholder may terminate unilaterally` c MEANS
        c's `the factors the premium is based on changed so that the insured risk fell`
    AND NOT c's `the insurer accepted the policyholder's request`
    AND c's `the terminating party notified the other immediately in writing`

@@q 584 587
@ref Dieu 23 (src:584-587)
GIVEN c IS A `A change in the insured risk`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 23(4): the insurer may terminate unilaterally` c MEANS
        c's `the factors the premium is based on changed so that the insured risk rose`
    AND NOT c's `the policyholder accepted the insurer's request`
    AND c's `the terminating party notified the other immediately in writing`

§§ `Dieu 24: interpretation`

-- Dieu 24. An unclear term with different readings is read in the policyholder's favour. The
-- function answers whose favour, and declines where the term is not unclear.
@@q 589 591
@ref Dieu 24 (src:589-591)
GIVEN `the term is unclear and has different readings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A party to the contract`
`Dieu 24: the party in whose favour the term is read` `the term is unclear and has different readings` MEANS
    IF `the term is unclear and has different readings`
    THEN `the policyholder`
    ELSE REFUSE "Dieu 24 applies only to a term that is unclear and has different readings"

§§ `Dieu 25: void contracts`

-- Dieu 25(1). The contract is void on any one of twelve grounds. Point (e) reads the policyholder's
-- status off the person; point (g) has an exception where the purpose was achieved or the mistake can
-- be cured at once; point (h) has an exception for the case dealt with in Dieu 22.
@@q 593 618
@ref Dieu 25 (src:593-618)
GIVEN f IS A `The formation of a contract`
      p IS A `A person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 25(1): the contract is void` f p MEANS
        f's `the policyholder had no insurable interest at the time of making`
    OR  f's `there was no object of insurance at the time of making`
    OR  f's `the policyholder knew the insured event had already occurred`
    OR  f's `the purpose or content violates a prohibition of law or social morality`
    OR  f's `the contract was a sham made by the insurer and the policyholder`
    OR  `the policyholder is a person Dieu 25(1)(e) names` p
    OR  (    f's `a mistake meant a party or both could not achieve the purpose of the contract`
         AND NOT f's `the purpose has been achieved or the mistake can be cured at once so that the purpose is still achieved`)
    OR  (f's `the contract was made as a result of deceit` AND NOT f's `the deceit is the deliberate conduct dealt with in Dieu 22`)
    OR  f's `the contract was made under threat or coercion`
    OR  f's `the policyholder did not understand and control own conduct when making it`
    OR  f's `the form required by Dieu 18 was not observed`

@@q 603 605
@ref Dieu 25 (src:603-605)
GIVEN p IS A `A person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the policyholder is a person Dieu 25(1)(e) names` p MEANS
        p's `is a minor`
    OR  p's `has lost civil act capacity`
    OR  p's `has difficulty in cognition or in controlling behaviour`
    OR  p's `has limited civil act capacity`

-- Dieu 25(2). A void contract has no effect from the time it was made; each side returns what it
-- received; the party at fault compensates.
@@q 619 622
@ref Dieu 25 (src:619-622)
GIVEN c IS A `A contract of insurance`
GIVETH A DATE
`Dieu 25(2): the date from which a void contract has no effect` c MEANS
    c's `date the contract was made`

§§ `Dieu 26: unilateral termination`

-- Dieu 26. The four grounds. The Law does not say which side may use each; the allocation below is
-- the one the ground itself implies (fork F8).
@@q 624 635
@ref Dieu 26 (src:624-635)
GIVEN g IS A `A ground for unilateral termination`
      p IS A `A party to the contract`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 26: the party has the right to terminate on the ground` g p MEANS
    CONSIDER g
    WHEN `premium not paid, or not paid in full, by the agreed time or after the grace period` THEN p EQUALS `the insurer`
    WHEN `a request to change the insured risk under Dieu 23 was not accepted`               THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the insured person did not take the safety measures of Dieu 55(3)`                 THEN p EQUALS `the insurer`
    WHEN `the policyholder did not agree to the transfer of the portfolio under Dieu 92(4)`  THEN p EQUALS `the policyholder`

§§ `Dieu 27: consequences of unilateral termination`

-- Dieu 27(1)(a). The policyholder must still pay premium up to termination, but not under an
-- individual life or health contract (a group contract is the exception to that exception).
@@q 638 645
@ref Dieu 27 (src:638-645)
GIVEN t IS A `A unilateral termination`
      c IS A `A contract of insurance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 27(1)(a): the policyholder must still pay premium up to termination` t c MEANS
        t's `ground` EQUALS `premium not paid, or not paid in full, by the agreed time or after the grace period`
    AND (    NOT (c's `class of contract` EQUALS `a life insurance contract` OR c's `class of contract` EQUALS `a health insurance contract`)
         OR  c's `is a group contract`)

-- Dieu 27(1)(b)-(c), 27(2): the insurer pays for an insured event that occurred before the
-- termination, on grounds 1, 2 and 3; Dieu 27(4) is silent for ground 4.
@@q 646 665
@ref Dieu 27 (src:646-665)
GIVEN t IS A `A unilateral termination`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 27: the insurer must pay for an insured event before termination` t MEANS
    CONSIDER t's `ground`
    WHEN `premium not paid, or not paid in full, by the agreed time or after the grace period` THEN t's `insured event occurred before termination`
    WHEN `a request to change the insured risk under Dieu 23 was not accepted`               THEN t's `insured event occurred before termination`
    WHEN `the insured person did not take the safety measures of Dieu 55(3)`                 THEN t's `insured event occurred before termination`
    WHEN `the policyholder did not agree to the transfer of the portfolio under Dieu 92(4)`  THEN REFUSE "Dieu 27(4) does not say whether an insured event before the termination is paid"

-- Dieu 27(2). On grounds 2 and 3 the insurer refunds the premium paid for the remaining period as
-- the contract agrees; the agreed refund is taken as the premium paid for that period (F13).
@@q 658 662
@ref Dieu 27 (src:658-662)
GIVEN t IS A `A unilateral termination`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Dieu 27(2): the premium the insurer must refund for the remaining period` t MEANS
    CONSIDER t's `ground`
    WHEN `a request to change the insured risk under Dieu 23 was not accepted`               THEN t's `premium paid for the period after termination`
    WHEN `the insured person did not take the safety measures of Dieu 55(3)`                 THEN t's `premium paid for the period after termination`
    OTHERWISE REFUSE "Dieu 27(2) refunds premium only on the grounds of Dieu 26(2) and 26(3)"

-- Dieu 27(3). On grounds 1 and 2, a life contract with a surrender value is paid that value unless
-- the parties agree otherwise (then the agreed amount is not known to the Law).
@@q 666 669
@ref Dieu 27 (src:666-669)
GIVEN t IS A `A unilateral termination`
      c IS A `A contract of insurance`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Dieu 27(3): the surrender value the insurer must pay` t c MEANS
    IF NOT (   t's `ground` EQUALS `premium not paid, or not paid in full, by the agreed time or after the grace period`
            OR t's `ground` EQUALS `a request to change the insured risk under Dieu 23 was not accepted`)
       OR NOT (c's `class of contract` EQUALS `a life insurance contract`)
       OR NOT t's `the contract has a surrender value`
    THEN REFUSE "Dieu 27(3) applies to a life contract with a surrender value terminated on the grounds of Dieu 26(1) or 26(2)"
    ELSE IF t's `the parties agreed otherwise on the surrender value`
         THEN REFUSE "Dieu 27(3): the parties agreed otherwise and the Law does not give the agreed amount"
         ELSE t's `surrender value`

-- Dieu 27(4). On ground 4 the policyholder gets back the surrender value or the premium for the
-- remaining period, and, if the transferred assets are less than the technical reserve of the
-- portfolio, that amount in the ratio of the assets to the reserve.
@@q 670 678
@ref Dieu 27 (src:670-678)
GIVEN t IS A `A unilateral termination`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Dieu 27(4): the amount the policyholder receives back` t MEANS
    IF NOT t's `ground` EQUALS `the policyholder did not agree to the transfer of the portfolio under Dieu 92(4)`
    THEN REFUSE "Dieu 27(4) applies to a termination on the ground of Dieu 26(4)"
    ELSE IF t's `technical reserve of the transferred portfolio` AT MOST 0
         THEN REFUSE "Dieu 27(4): the technical reserve of the transferred portfolio is not positive"
         ELSE IF t's `value of the transferred assets` AT LEAST t's `technical reserve of the transferred portfolio`
              THEN `the amount before the ratio` t
              ELSE `the amount before the ratio` t TIMES t's `value of the transferred assets` DIVIDED BY t's `technical reserve of the transferred portfolio`

GIVEN t IS A `A unilateral termination`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount before the ratio` t MEANS
    IF t's `the contract has a surrender value` THEN t's `surrender value` ELSE t's `premium paid for the period after termination`

§§ `Dieu 28: transfer of the contract`

-- Dieu 28. The policyholder may transfer; a life contract needs the insured person's written
-- consent; the transferee needs an insurable interest; it takes effect only on written notice and
-- the insurer's written agreement, unless made under international custom or the contract (F9).
@@q 680 689
@ref Dieu 28 (src:680-689)
GIVEN t IS A `A transfer of a contract`
      c IS A `A contract of insurance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 28: the transfer takes effect` t c MEANS
        (   NOT c's `class of contract` EQUALS `a life insurance contract`
         OR t's `the insured person or the insured person's legal representative agreed in writing`)
    AND t's `the transferee has an insurable interest`
    AND (   t's `the transfer is made under international custom or by agreement in the contract`
         OR (t's `the policyholder notified the insurer in writing` AND t's `the insurer agreed in writing`))

§§ `Dieu 29: reinsurance does not change the insurer's liability`

@@q 691 697
@ref Dieu 29 (src:691-697)
GIVEN r IS A `A reinsurance in the background of a contract`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 29(1): the insurer's refusal or delay breaches Dieu 29(1)` r MEANS
    r's `the insurer refused or delayed performing for the policyholder` AND r's `the reinsurer did not meet its obligation to the insurer`

@@q 698 700
@ref Dieu 29 (src:698-700)
GIVEN r IS A `A reinsurance in the background of a contract`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 29(2): the reinsurer's demand for premium breaches Dieu 29(2)` r MEANS
    r's `the reinsurer asked the policyholder to pay premium directly to it` AND NOT r's `the contract agrees otherwise`

@@q 701 703
@ref Dieu 29 (src:701-703)
GIVEN r IS A `A reinsurance in the background of a contract`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 29(3): the policyholder's demand on the reinsurer breaches Dieu 29(3)` r MEANS
    r's `the policyholder asked the reinsurer to pay the insurance money to it` AND NOT r's `the contract agrees otherwise`

§§ `Dieu 30: time for submitting the claim dossier`

-- Dieu 30. One year from the insured event; force majeure days do not count; from the day the claimant
-- learned of the event if they prove they did not know when it occurred; from the third person's claim
-- on the policyholder where that is the claim. The last day is the anniversary of the starting day,
-- plus the days of force majeure (F10, F11).
@@q 707 717
@ref Dieu 30 (src:707-717)
GIVEN c IS A `A claim`
GIVETH A DATE
`Dieu 30: the day from which the year runs` c MEANS
    BRANCH IF c's `a third person claimed compensation from the policyholder` THEN c's `date of the third person's claim`
           IF c's `the claimant proves they did not know when the insured event occurred` THEN c's `date the insured person or beneficiary learned of the insured event`
           OTHERWISE c's `date of the insured event`

GIVEN c IS A `A claim`
GIVETH A DATE
`Dieu 30: the last day for submitting the claim dossier` c MEANS
    (`add years` (`Dieu 30: the day from which the year runs` c) 1) PLUS c's `days of force majeure or objective obstacle`

GIVEN c IS A `A claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 30: the dossier was submitted in time` c MEANS
    c's `date the claim dossier was submitted` AT MOST `Dieu 30: the last day for submitting the claim dossier` c

§§ `Dieu 31: time for paying`

-- Dieu 31(1). Pay within the time agreed in the contract; if none, within 15 days from the day the
-- full and valid dossier is received. Dieu 31(2): interest on a late payment for the time of delay, at
-- the rate the parties agree under the Civil Code (an input; the Law gives no rate, and the rate is
-- taken as a rate per day, F12).
@@q 719 724
@ref Dieu 31 (src:719-724)
GIVEN c IS A `A claim`
GIVETH A DATE
`Dieu 31(1): the last day for the insurer to pay` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `days agreed in the contract for payment`
    WHEN JUST n THEN c's `date the insurer received the full and valid dossier` PLUS n
    WHEN NOTHING THEN c's `date the insurer received the full and valid dossier` PLUS 15

@@q 725 729
@ref Dieu 31 (src:725-729)
GIVEN c IS A `A claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Dieu 31(2): the days of delay` c MEANS
    max 0 (Day (c's `date the insurer paid`) MINUS Day (`Dieu 31(1): the last day for the insurer to pay` c))

GIVEN c IS A `A claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Dieu 31(2): the interest on the late payment` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `daily interest rate agreed under the Civil Code`
    WHEN JUST r THEN c's `amount paid late` TIMES r TIMES `Dieu 31(2): the days of delay` c
    WHEN NOTHING THEN REFUSE "Dieu 31(2) fixes the interest rate by agreement of the parties under the Civil Code; no rate is supplied"

§§ `Dieu 32: resolving disputes`

@@q 731 734
@ref Dieu 32 (src:731-734)
GIVEN d IS A `A dispute on a contract`
GIVETH A MAYBE `A forum for a dispute`
`Dieu 32: the forum for the dispute` d MEANS
    IF d's `the parties negotiated successfully`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER d's `forum agreed in the contract`
         WHEN JUST f THEN JUST f
         WHEN NOTHING THEN REFUSE "Dieu 32: negotiation failed and the contract names no forum; the Law leaves mediation, arbitration or court to the contract"
